---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Foundation Repair in Hideaway, TX | Tyler Foundation Pros"
  description="Foundation repair for Hideaway Lake homeowners in East Texas. We connect you with expert pier & beam and slab repair contractors. Free inspection. Call (903) 582-7837."
>
  <HeroSection
    h1="Foundation Repair in Hideaway, TX"
    subheading="Specialized foundation repair contractors for Hideaway's older pier-and-beam homes. Free inspections, local expertise."
    buttonText="Call (903) 582-7837 — Free Hideaway Inspection"
  />

  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg mb-4">
        Hideaway is one of East Texas's most distinctive communities — a gated lake community with older homes, mature trees, and a tight-knit neighborhood feel. It's also a community with some of the most specialized foundation repair needs in Smith County.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg">
        The majority of Hideaway's older homes are built on pier-and-beam foundations. After decades of East Texas humidity, seasonal moisture changes, and soil movement near the lake, many of these homes have developed significant foundation issues that require expert, experienced repair.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8">Why Hideaway Homes Need Specialized Foundation Care</h2>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Proximity to Water</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Homes near Hideaway Lake and its feeder creeks experience more consistent soil moisture — but also more dramatic fluctuations when water levels drop during drought. This accelerates foundation movement compared to homes on drier sites.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Age of Construction</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Most Hideaway homes were built in the 1970s through 1990s. Pier-and-beam foundations from this era typically used wood piers and beams that are now reaching or past their service life. Inspection is critical for any home in this age range.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Tree Root Activity</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Mature trees throughout Hideaway aggressively seek moisture, and their root systems can draw water from directly beneath pier-and-beam foundations — causing soil to dry and compact unevenly and leading to differential settlement.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-14 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Pier &amp; Beam Specialists for Hideaway</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Because pier-and-beam repair is the predominant need in Hideaway, we connect you with contractors who have specialized experience with crawl space access, beam sistering, pier replacement, and moisture barrier installation — contractors who know East Texas crawl spaces and what to look for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    heading="Schedule Your Free Hideaway Inspection"
    subtext="Specialized pier-and-beam contractors for Hideaway Lake homes. Free inspection, no pressure."
    buttonText="Call (903) 582-7837 — Free Hideaway Inspection"
  />
</Layout>
